21.14 Resource limits

Centralized hard limits cover:
- total input bytes;
- decompressed bytes;
- IR step count;
- selector depth;
- parsed structure depth;
- collection size;
- regex pattern size;
- regex input size;
- worker execution duration;
- archive expansion where applicable.

The implementation selects explicit constants, centralizes them, documents them, and regression-tests every boundary.
Limits must not be scattered throughout the code.

35.3 Artifact bytes

Actual artifact Blobs are:
- stored;
- hashed on intake;
- read back;
- rehashed;
- marked unavailable when verification fails.

Byte-dependent work blocks when bytes are unavailable or unverified.

35.4 Storage status

At startup, the application should request persistent storage and estimate quota.
The result is displayed honestly.
Browser-local storage is not represented as protection from device, browser-profile, or browser loss.

